### Specifications API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for specification tags management endpoints
### All operations for creating, reading, updating, and deleting specifications

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@specificationId = your-specification-uuid-here

### ============================================
### VARIABLES SETUP
### ============================================
### Replace the variables above with actual values:
### - @token: JWT token from /api/auth/verify-otp (if authentication is required)
### - @specificationId: UUID of an existing specification

### ============================================
### 1. CREATE SPECIFICATION
### ============================================
### Create a new specification tag
### Public endpoint (authentication may be required based on your setup)
### Both name and icon are required

POST {{baseUrl}}/specifications
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Web Development",
  "icon": "web-icon"
}

### Example: Create Another Specification
POST {{baseUrl}}/specifications
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Mobile Development",
  "icon": "mobile-icon"
}

### Example: Create Design Specification
POST {{baseUrl}}/specifications
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Graphic Design",
  "icon": "design-icon"
}

### Response Example (201 Created):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Specification created successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "specification-uuid",
###     "name": "Web Development",
###     "icon": "web-icon",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 2. GET ALL SPECIFICATIONS
### ============================================
### Get all specifications with pagination and optional search
### Public endpoint (no authentication required)
### Query Parameters:
###   - page: Page number (default: 1)
###   - limit: Items per page (default: 100, max: 500)
###   - search: Search term to filter specifications by name (optional)

### Get All Specifications (Default - First Page, 100 items)
GET {{baseUrl}}/specifications
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Specifications with Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/specifications?page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Specifications with Search
GET {{baseUrl}}/specifications?page=1&limit=10&search=web
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Specifications - Second Page
GET {{baseUrl}}/specifications?page=2&limit=20
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Specifications fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "id": "specification-uuid",
###       "name": "Web Development",
###       "icon": "web-icon",
###       "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###     }
###   ],
###   "pagination": {
###     "page": 1,
###     "limit": 10,
###     "totalPages": 5,
###     "totalItems": 50,
###     "hasNextPage": true,
###     "hasPreviousPage": false
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 3. GET SPECIFICATION BY ID
### ============================================
### Get a specific specification by its ID
### Public endpoint (no authentication required)

GET {{baseUrl}}/specifications/{{specificationId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Specification fetched successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "specification-uuid",
###     "name": "Web Development",
###     "icon": "web-icon",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 4. UPDATE SPECIFICATION
### ============================================
### Update an existing specification
### Public endpoint (authentication may be required based on your setup)
### At least one field must be provided for update

PUT {{baseUrl}}/specifications/{{specificationId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Full Stack Web Development"
}

### Example: Update Specification Name and Icon
PUT {{baseUrl}}/specifications/{{specificationId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Modern Web Development",
  "icon": "modern-web-icon"
}

### Example: Update Only Icon
PUT {{baseUrl}}/specifications/{{specificationId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "icon": "updated-icon"
}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Specification updated successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "specification-uuid",
###     "name": "Full Stack Web Development",
###     "icon": "web-icon",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T02:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 5. DELETE SPECIFICATION
### ============================================
### Delete a specification by ID
### Public endpoint (authentication may be required based on your setup)
### Note: Consider impact on linked skills before deleting

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/specifications/{{specificationId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Specification deleted successfully"
### }

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - Check your route configuration to see if authentication is required
###    - If authentication is required, use: Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
###    - Get token from: POST /api/auth/verify-otp

### 2. VALIDATION RULES
###    Create Specification:
###    - name: Required, string, 1-100 characters
###    - icon: Required, string, minimum 1 character
###    
###    Update Specification:
###    - At least one field must be provided
###    - name: Optional, string, 1-100 characters if provided
###    - icon: Optional, string, minimum 1 character if provided

### 3. PAGINATION
###    - Default page: 1
###    - Default limit: 100
###    - Maximum limit: 500
###    - Search is case-insensitive and searches specification names

### 4. RELATIONSHIP WITH SKILLS
###    - Specifications can have multiple skills linked to them
###    - Skills reference specifications via specificationId
###    - When deleting a specification, consider impact on linked skills
###    - Skills can exist without a specification (specificationId: null)

### 5. ERROR RESPONSES
###    
###    Validation Error (400):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Validation error message",
###      "errors": [
###        {
###          "field": "name",
###          "message": "Specification name is required"
###        }
###      ]
###    }
###    
###    Not Found (404):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Specification not found"
###    }

### 6. SUCCESS RESPONSES
###    
###    Create Specification (201):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Specification created successfully",
###       "data": { ... }
###     }
###    
###    Get Specifications (200):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Specifications fetched successfully",
###       "data": [ ... ],
###       "pagination": { ... }
###     }
###    
###    Update Specification (200):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Specification updated successfully",
###       "data": { ... }
###     }
###    
###    Delete Specification (200):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Specification deleted successfully"
###     }

### 7. BEST PRACTICES
###    - Use clear, descriptive specification names
###    - Use consistent icon naming conventions
###    - Group related skills under appropriate specifications
###    - Search for existing specifications before creating duplicates
###    - Update specifications rather than creating duplicates
###    - Consider impact on linked skills before deleting

### 8. COMMON USE CASES
###    
###    Case 1: Create a new specification category
###    1. POST /api/specifications with name and icon
###    2. Specification is created
###    3. Link skills to this specification using PUT /api/skills/:id
###    
###    Case 2: Search for specifications
###    1. GET /api/specifications?search=web
###    2. Returns matching specifications with pagination
###    
###    Case 3: Update specification details
###    1. PUT /api/specifications/:id with updated fields
###    2. Specification is updated
###    
###    Case 4: Reorganize skills by specification
###    1. Get all specifications: GET /api/specifications
###    2. Update skills to link to appropriate specifications
###    3. Use PUT /api/skills/:id with specificationId

### ============================================
### TESTING EXAMPLES
### ============================================

### Test: Create Specification with Long Name
POST {{baseUrl}}/specifications
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Full Stack Web Development and Mobile Applications",
  "icon": "fullstack-icon"
}

### Test: Search Specifications
GET {{baseUrl}}/specifications?search=mobile&page=1&limit=5
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Test: Update Only Name
PUT {{baseUrl}}/specifications/{{specificationId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Updated Specification Name"
}

### Test: Update Only Icon
PUT {{baseUrl}}/specifications/{{specificationId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "icon": "new-icon-name"
}

### Test: Update Both Fields
PUT {{baseUrl}}/specifications/{{specificationId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Modern Web Technologies",
  "icon": "modern-icon"
}
